   "source": [
    "# Importing necessary libraries\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Games of Chance\n",
    "Games of chance involve randomness and probability. Examples include rolling dice, spinning a roulette wheel, or drawing cards from a shuffled deck."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Simulating a dice roll\n",
    "dice_rolls = np.random.randint(1, 7, 1000)\n",
    "plt.hist(dice_rolls, bins=np.arange(1, 8)-0.5, edgecolor='black')\n",
    "plt.xlabel('Dice Value')\n",
    "plt.ylabel('Frequency')\n",
    "plt.title('Dice Roll Simulation')\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Games of Skill\n",
    "Games of skill require strategy and decision-making. Examples include chess, poker, and video games."
